  "result": "This file (`src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`) contains both the retry ceiling and the backoff growth for webhook deliveries — the case matching \"customer's receiving server was down\":\n\n- `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` (line 22) — the cap; deliveries past this are marked failed for good (`delivery.attempts > MAX_ATTEMPTS`, line 49).\n- `backoffMs(attempts)` (line 90) — exponential backoff: `2^(attempts-1) * 1000ms`, capped at 300,000ms (5 minutes), so it doubles each retry (1s, 2s, 4s, …) until it plateaus.\n\nNote there's a similarly-named `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5` in `src/config/constants.ts`, but it's unused dead code (only referenced in a manifest generator script, never imported by the job) — the job defines and uses its own local `MAX_ATTEMPTS`, so that constants file isn't actually part of the retry behavior.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
